The '''Pokémon School''' (Japanese: '''ポケモンスクール''' ''Pokémon School'') is an {{pkmn|animated series}}-exclusive [[Pokémon academy]] in the [[Alola]] [[region]]. It first appeared in ''[[SM001|Alola to New Adventure!]]'' and is one of the main settings of ''[[Pokémon the Series: Sun & Moon]]''. The school is located on [[Melemele Island]]. In ''[[SM042|Alola, Kanto!]]'', the school celebrated its 20th anniversary. Sometime after ''[[SM055|The Professors' New Adventure!]]'', the school was converted to be the base for the [[Ultra Guardians]], which was first put to use in ''[[SM061|A Mission of Ultra Urgency!]]''.

==In animation==
===''[[Pokémon the Series: Sun & Moon]]''===
[[File:Pokémon School class.png|thumb|250px|The class]]
[[File:Ultra Ruin Pokemon School.png|thumb|250px|The Ultra Ruin Pokémon School]]
The Pokémon School first appeared in ''[[SM001|Alola to New Adventure!]]'', where {{Ash}} and {{Delia}} were tasked by {{an|Professor Oak}} to deliver an {{pkmn|Egg}} to [[Samson Oak]]. After meeting {{an|Professor Kukui}} and several of the students, Ash opted to remain in Alola and study.

The Pokémon School held an open house event during ''[[SM024|Alolan Open House!]]'', where a number of the students' families turned up. Ash was tasked with giving a presentation in front of everyone.

The Pokémon School celebrated its 20th anniversary during ''[[SM042|Alola, Kanto!]]'', which saw the class taking a field trip to [[Kanto]].

An alternate version of the Pokémon School was shown in the [[Ultra Ruin]] in ''[[SM100|Battling the Beast Within!]]'' and ''[[SM101|Parallel Friendships!]]''. It is currently the home of {{al|Dia}}.

===''[[Pokémon Journeys: The Series]]''===
In ''[[JN037|That New Old Gang of Mine!]]'', Ash and [[Goh]] attended a welcome party at the Pokémon School arranged by Mallow and the others. Goh later {{pkmn|battle}}d {{an|Kiawe}} and {{TP|Kiawe|Turtonator}}, but the battle was called off after Kiawe used {{m|Inferno Overdrive}}.

In ''[[JN131|Paring Pokémon While Parrying!]]'', Ash's classmates, Alolan Pokémon, {{an|Gladion}}, Samson Oak, Professor Kukui, {{an|Professor Burnet}}, and [[Lei]] were all seen watching Ash's [[Masters Eight Tournament]] match against {{an|Leon}} at the Pokémon School.
